# pyiv requirements (for application code)

Copy into your project's `.cursor/rules/` (or equivalent) when the app depends on pyiv.

- Prefer `from pyiv import …` for featured types (`Config`, `get_injector`,
  `Filesystem`, `Clock`, `Logger`, `Environment`, `HttpClient`, …).
- Wire graphs with `Config.configure` / Binder; inject via constructors.
- Depend on injectables instead of calling `open`, `time.sleep`, `os.environ`,
  `subprocess`, or `logging.getLogger` at owned call sites.
- In tests, bind Memory/Synthetic doubles — do not monkeypatch those stdlib edges.
- Option bags: `@dataclass(frozen=True)` with boring field types; services:
  Protocol/ABC + Real/Fake bindings.
- Core `pyiv` is stdlib-only; use `pyiv-common` only for YAML/requests.

